The four forge comments are already implemented on this branch, and the suite that covers them passes.

**Tool routing.** `_infer_tool` checks `get employee <id>` and `get sales order <id>` before the list heuristics, and puts the id in `tool_args`. `get employee emp-001` goes to `get_employee_by_id` with `{"id": "emp-001"}` instead of `list_employees`.

**FastMCP SSE.** Tool-call tests talk to an in-process SSE peer. A JSON-RPC POST to the SSE URL is rejected. The client must GET `/sse` with `Accept: text/event-stream`, initialize the session, and POST `tools/call` to the message endpoint.

**Four tools and id normalization.** `list_sales_order`, `list_employees`, `get_employee_by_id` (`emp-001` → `EMP-001`), and `get_sales_order_by_id` (`so-123` → `SO-123`) are all asserted on that SSE session.

**Health probe.** `/health` uses the same GET and `Accept: text/event-stream` headers as the MCP client. The fake server answers HEAD with 501, and the up-check still reports `mcp_reachable: true`.

`pytest` — 32 passed.

