The project virtualenv is at `.venv` in this worktree. The story tests were already run with that interpreter, and all 37 passed.
The original stdio agent uppercased every string `id` with `value.upper()` and no format check. `emp001` and `ord-001` were already supported, so `_normalize_id()` keeps that behavior and the hyphen-only restriction was not added.

Supported forms, all sent uppercased:

| Input | Sent to the tool |
|---|---|
| `emp-001`, `Emp-001`, `EMP-001` | `EMP-001` |
| `emp001`, `Emp001`, `EMP001` | `EMP001` |
| `so-123`, `SO-123` | `SO-123` |
| `so123` | `SO123` |
| `ord-001`, `Ord-001` | `ORD-001` |

The LLM returns the id as written. `mcp_client._normalize_id()` uppercases it before the FastMCP call. The setup section of the README shows these examples. Hub specs were left unchanged. 58 tests passed.

