Entity-by-id questions now stay on `get_employee_by_id` and `get_sales_order_by_id`, and the id from the question is kept.

`agent/llm_client.py` matches those two questions before the model’s tool choice is accepted. If the model picks a list tool, omits `id`, or answers in prose, the handler still sends the matching get-by-id tool with the raw id (`emp-001`, `emp001`, `Emp-001`, `so-123`, `so123`, `ord-001`). Uppercasing stays in `agent/mcp_client.py`. List and greeting questions are unchanged and still follow the model.

`tests/test_tool_inference.py` covers that override. The full suite is **68 passed**. No further file edits were required; this behavior is already in the working tree.
The tool-call test now checks the real FastMCP SSE handshake, so a plain JSON-RPC POST cannot pass it.

`tests/test_tool_call.py` starts the official FastMCP SSE server and leaves `sse_client` unpatched. For each of the four tools it requires:

- `GET /sse` with `Accept: text/event-stream` before any POST
- no JSON-RPC POST to the SSE URL
- `initialize`, then `notifications/initialized`, then `tools/call` on the session `/messages` URL
- the call arguments the server actually receives (`emp-001` becomes `EMP-001`, `so-123` becomes `SO-123`)

The story 02 query path was already in place: direct answers, tool routing, and `{"error": "LLM unavailable"}`.

All 68 tests passed. File changed: `tests/test_tool_call.py`.
Story 02 now keeps the original ID contract. Every string `id` is uppercased, including unhyphenated forms, and the question parser no longer drops IDs that fall outside a hyphenated `prefix-digits` pattern.

The original stdio orchestrator used `value.upper()` whenever the argument key was `id`. There was no format check, so `emp001`, `foo-bar-123`, `emp_001`, and `001` were all in scope. `agent/mcp_client.py` still does that uppercasing before the FastMCP call. `agent/llm_client.py` only extracts the raw token with `[\w-]+` and leaves normalization to the client.

